        <briefdescription>
<para>Computes an SDBM 64-bit hash over an arbitrary byte range. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Implements the SDBM hash algorithm (originating from the sdbm database library). For each element <computeroutput>c:</computeroutput> <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">h<sp/>=<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">static_cast&lt;</highlight><highlight class="normal">std::uint8_t</highlight><highlight class="keyword">&gt;</highlight><highlight class="normal">(c)<sp/>+<sp/>(h<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/>6)<sp/>+<sp/>(h<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/>16)<sp/>-<sp/>h;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>SDBM is known for good distribution across short keys and is widely used in database and compiler applications.</para>
<para>The function is <computeroutput>constexpr</computeroutput>, allowing compile-time hash computation.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para><bold>Chaining:</bold> pass the result of a previous call as <computeroutput>h:</computeroutput> <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>h<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__scl__utility__hash_1gaec361ebf99797481bbe413b6faf9d7e0" kindref="member">scl::hash::sdbm</ref>(first_range);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">h<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="group__scl__utility__hash_1gaec361ebf99797481bbe413b6faf9d7e0" kindref="member">scl::hash::sdbm</ref>(second_range,<sp/>h);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</simplesect>
